===== reading (this chunk's verdict, current build):
* Engine ran (`live`): every output is a **conforming linearized file** — the parameter dictionary at byte 27
  (inside the first 1024), `/L` equal to the file length to the byte, `/H` naming a real object carrying the `/S`
  hint dictionary, the first page's object (`/O`) before the second group and before `/E ≤ /T`, **two** cross-reference
  sections, and `libqpdf` (pikepdf 10.9.1 = qpdf 12.3.2's own library — there is no `qpdf` binary in this box,
  recorded substitution) reporting `check_linearization()` ok. Ghostscript re-opens all four with exit 0 and MuPDF
  reads them at the right page count. Nothing is lost: ink and characters equal per page, on text, image-heavy,
  annotated and already-linearized inputs.
* Engine blocked (`block`): the card says `ENGINE local path · qpdf not used`, the sentence ends
  “This is not a conforming linearized PDF.”, the warning names the URL and the failure
  (`qpdf could not be reached (Failed to load qpdf from https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/qpdf-wasm@0.1.0/: Failed to fetch),
  so this file was rebuilt locally and is not linearized`), and the bytes agree: no `/Linearized` dictionary at all,
  one cross-reference section (an xref stream), libqpdf refuses it — judged by `linearize-check.py --fallback`, which
  is the mode for “the engine never ran”; `--before` is the *other* case (a dictionary written and lying).
* Fast Web View, measured rather than read: see the prefix section above. The engine's output puts every object sheet 1
  needs, plus the hint stream, inside the `/E` byte it promises — 2 466 of 5 978 B (41 %) on colour.pdf and 2 696 of
  82 274 B (3.3 %) on heavy.pdf — while the same documents' non-linearized forms need the whole page-tree walk
  (88.3 % and 3.2 %→99 % by tree order). The `PAGES 8 in · out not counted` row is honest for the engine branch (qpdf
  hands back a finished file and no document), and the rebuild counts pages normally.
* Encrypted input (`locked.pdf`): no file, no crash, the card asks for the password by name and offers Retry.
* A file that grows is warned, not hidden: “The file came out bigger than the one you started with. Nothing was
  overwritten — download the original unless you need this variant.” (colour +12 %, annot +14 %, heavy +1 %).
* Network half: 8/8 runs, 0 file bytes posted anywhere; the only off-origin traffic is Google Fonts CSS/woff2 for the
  shell and, when not blocked, `qpdf.js` + `qpdf.wasm` from cdn.jsdelivr.net — the documented engine fetch.
